@* Ported from Index.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs (CRM module landing control,
   reached through the host's /Modules/{*path} route).

   FAITHFULNESS NOTE - this control is content-free BY ORIGIN, not by omission:
     * Index.ascx contained ONLY the license comment and the <%@ Control %> directive -
       no server control, no literal, no markup at all.
     * Index.ascx.designer.cs declared NO fields (no placeholder to populate).
     * Index.ascx.cs overrode OnControlLoad with an EMPTY body and declared no
       OverridePath, AccessLevel, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme or IsLandingPage override,
       and implemented no ITransaction.
   So the original rendered an empty region, and the whole of its server-side behaviour is
   the base class's logging + the two authorization checks, which MixERPUserControl runs.
   Emitting any markup here would ADD a screen the module never had. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl

@code {

    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control must declare
    ///     it. The legacy override of this control had an empty body (verified against
    ///     Index.ascx.cs), and the base raises it from OnInitialized exactly once, as the
    ///     WebForms Load event did.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }
}
